<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen down 11 bps.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen down 11 bps.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 0.11 basis points to 18.80 percent, and rates are also seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     18.91	    18.80		  - 11 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     20.79	    20.58		  - 21 bps</p>
<p>    181-DAY    21.85	    21.64		  - 21 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     23.06	    22.92		  - 14 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 local (2330 GMT).</p>
<p>((--Elena Vega, Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559))</p>
